  custom_function              declines: unsupported for majit lowering: call `add`

per-row cost BY TIER — one replicated-batch slope, run on three tiers.
`interp` is the traced portal with its trace threshold at `u32::MAX`, so it can
never compile: that column is the per-row cost BEFORE compiling and `jit` is the
same row AFTER. `clean` is the same columnar program on the batch machine's
UNTRACED interpreter, the floor under both.

⚠ `clean` is NOT `cel::vm`. It is `BoundBatch::collect_on(Tier::Clean)`, a plain
`match` interpreter over the LOWERED columnar code — registers and banks over
flattened `ColumnRef` buffers. No `Value`, no `Arc`, no stack. The VM column on
this board is `exec`, and it is the only one whose cost is about `interp.rs`.
